+# TODO
+
+## Unsmell run 2026-11-01 (seb.py, schema.sql)
+
+- `schema.sql:2` — the `iban` column also holds the Enable Banking uid when an account has no IBAN (`Account.key` in `seb.py`). A column that holds two kinds of identifier should be named for what it is, such as `account`. Renaming it needs a migration of the existing `dengi.db`, because `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` never changes a table that already exists.
+- `schema.sql:18` — `remittance` holds the JSON array `remittance_information` as text. Either name it for the array (`remittance_lines`) or store the lines joined, for example with `group_concat` over `json_each`. Both options change the stored schema.
+- `schema.sql:12` — `amount_cents` multiplies by 100, which assumes that the currency has two decimals. That holds for EUR. Choose between keeping the decimal string as `amount`, or scaling by the ISO 4217 exponent of `currency`.
+- `schema.sql:19` — the comment maps `bank_transaction_code.description` to the ISO 20022 domain. Check this against the Enable Banking `BankTransactionCode` schema. If `description` is free text, the `tx_code` column and its comment are both wrong.
+- `seb.py` `Config.from_env` — `EB_ASPSP` lets the user pick another bank, but `aspsp_country` is fixed at "LT" and the module doc and the schema comment assume SEB. Either drop `EB_ASPSP`, or add `EB_ASPSP_COUNTRY` and make the docs bank-neutral.
+- `schema.sql` — an existing `dengi.db` keeps its old table, so it lacks the new generated `is_debit` column. Nothing reads that column yet. Add a migration (for example `ALTER TABLE txn ADD COLUMN` guarded by `PRAGMA table_info`) before any query relies on it.
